sb4edge: variable refresh (VRR) for the eDP panel on X1E80100 through the DPU INTF AVR block
(the timing-engine half of Qualcomm's downstream "Qsync", sde_hw_intf.c avr_setup/avr_ctrl/avr_trigger).
Off unless msm.vrr=1|2 (with VRR_ENABLED, continuous|one-shot) or 3 (always): the eDP connector gets vrr_capable (DPCD
MSA_TIMING_PAR_IGNORED + EDID range), the sink is told to ignore MSA timing, and while the compositor sets
VRR_ENABLED the INTF stretches the front porch up to the EDID minimum refresh and each flushed frame triggers
the next one. Scanout position is clamped during the extended porch for vblank timestamps.

